CARRIED PATCH - fork content, not ours, and not upstream. Provenance and why,
for whoever reads this next.

Source: RyanDam/zephyr branch `v4.4.1+zmk-fixes` (the pin this workspace used
before moving to upstream v4.5.0). The commits below were cherry-picked onto
the v4.5.0 tag with `git cherry-pick -x`, so they are also history on the
`v4.5.0+coban-fixes` branch in the west checkout - this file is the copy that
survives a `west update`, which throws away the branch.

Commits, oldest first:
  f3ec35d5bc  Peter Johanson <peter@peterjohanson.com>  2025-11-01
            boards: seeed: xiao_ble: UF2 runner default, remove ID match
Why it is carried rather than dropped: the old pin had it and this one would
not, so a board that comes to depend on it would silently get a different
Zephyr. The pin is meant to be a drop-in for the branch it replaced, so the
whole delta moves with it rather than the parts today's boards happen to use.

